# Pin exact minimum source identities for `Simpsons.exe` and `Simpsons.ico`

The source manifest must express exact root-file identities in addition to
folder/type minimums. `Simpsons.exe` and `Simpsons.ico` are mandatory;
`uninst.ico` is explicitly optional and only relevant to some from-scratch
source/build workflows.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Require root `Simpsons.exe` by exact case-sensitive/canonical identity,
  minimum one.
- [ ] Require root `Simpsons.ico` by exact canonical identity, minimum one.
- [ ] Record root `uninst.ico` as optional with minimum zero.
- [ ] Make these requirements immutable schema authority rather than editable
  rows that can turn invalid source into valid source by lowering a count.
- [ ] Keep deep deterministic validation authoritative; this exact-file check is
  an early source gate, not a replacement for the reconstruction algorithm.
- [ ] Update README source-validation language when implementation lands.

## Dependencies

Coordinate with the canonical game-manifest validator and build preflight.

## Evidence

The planning contract reflects the real local source names observed today:
`Simpsons.exe`, `Simpsons.ico`, and `uninst.ico`.
